messages:
ryan: Heads-up: tried the official Redwood JS SDK in an Expo dev-client app (Hermes). Metro fails to bundle: "Unexpected token 'export'" coming from node_modules/redwood-inference/dist/index.mjs. App doesn't even load.

ellie: That sounds like Metro hitting an ESM-only file. Expo's Metro expects CJS unless you add extra config. What's the import line?

ryan: `import { createClient } from 'redwood-inference'` — which resolves to the package exports -> module (ESM). If I switch to `require('redwood-inference')` I get different errors (node:crypto unresolved).

mark: This is a messy intersection of three issues: (1) ESM packaging + Metro static analysis, (2) node: namespace imports in our ESM build, (3) RN runtime (Hermes) missing typical node globals (Buffer, atob). We've seen this with other SDKs.

ellie: Quick devrecipes that worked for me in Expo: 1) For ESM error, force Metro to prefer cjs by adding a resolver redirect OR require the CJS build directly. 2) Shim node libs and globals. Example metro.config.js patch:
```js
const path = require('path');
module.exports = {
  resolver: {
    extraNodeModules: {
      crypto: path.resolve(__dirname, 'node_modules', 'react-native-crypto'),
      'node:crypto': path.resolve(__dirname, 'node_modules', 'react-native-crypto'),
      stream: path.resolve(__dirname, 'node_modules', 'stream-browserify'),
      buffer: path.resolve(__dirname, 'node_modules', 'buffer'),
    },
    sourceExts: ['js', 'json', 'ts', 'tsx', 'jsx'],
  },
};
```
and in App.tsx top: `import 'react-native-get-random-values'; globalThis.Buffer = require('buffer').Buffer;`

ryan: That unblocked startup. But then we hit subtle runtime: fetch in RN (Expo) drops the Authorization header in some redirect flows and the SDK's retry logic retried on 401 which caused double requests and unexpected 429s from the backend.

esther: Important doc note: recommend SDK users in RN to 1) set auth explicitly on the client config (don't rely on background token refresh in some RN fetch polyfills), 2) configure retry policy to NOT retry on 401, and 3) prefer idempotent retry for GETs only. Example: `retries: { retries: 2, retryOn: (err, status) => status && status !== 401 }`.

mark: For DX we should add a `react-native` export in package.json that points to a tiny wrapper bundle (CJS or RN-friendly ESM) that avoids `node:` imports and only uses RN-safe shims. That would save a lot of per-app Metro hacks.

ellie: Agreed. Proposed wrapper pseudocode for SDK repo:
```js
// dist/react-native.js (small wrapper)
import 'react-native-get-random-values';
globalThis.Buffer = require('buffer').Buffer;
module.exports = require('./cjs'); // or a trimmed client that avoids node: imports
```
and package.json: "react-native": "dist/react-native.js" export.

ryan: Also about types: TS projects get noisy when you add @types/node to satisfy Buffer/Process types. Two options: 1) add a `global.d.ts` with minimal declarations (Buffer, btoa/atob), 2) include @types/node but set `skipLibCheck: true` to avoid collisions with react-native types. My team chose the global.d.ts to keep compile faster.

esther: I'll add a short RN troubleshooting section to the SDK README + an Expo sample app with metro config, tsconfig snippet, and a tested auth/retry example. We should also call out Hermes-specific caveats.

dev-bot: Created ticket #2102: "devex: Expo RN sample + react-native export + RN README (polyfills, metro, auth/retries)" assigned to @esther. :white_check_mark:

ryan: Thanks. If anyone wants to repro quickly: minimal repro steps in a new Expo app: 1) `npx expo init` -> blank (TS), 2) `yarn add redwood-inference react-native-get-random-values react-native-crypto buffer stream-browserify react-native-url-polyfill`, 3) apply metro.config and App imports above, 4) if you get ESM errors try `const Redwood = require('redwood-inference/dist/cjs')` as a temporary workaround. Paste crash logs here if anything else shows up. :pray:
